@H H_1163 := "the H_1160 RESIDUAL — does the DERIVATIVE-gated mitosis TICK beat METRONOME and POSITIONAL on a STAGE-DECODE / RECON-FIDELITY metric (NOT next-step prediction), with a phase-shuffle control?" :: discovery [d=2026-06-12 status=🔴-CLOSED-NEGATIVE domain=MITOSIS-ENGINE]

  seed = "H_1160 (🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE) found the cell-division split-trigger gate {METRONOME, POSITIONAL, DERIVATIVE, NOGATE} gives NO advantage on the substrate-native ONLINE NEXT-STEP PREDICTION ERROR metric (all 4 tie within noise). But H_1160's honest residual was explicit: 'a next-step-error metric is the WRONG instrument to detect a tick-placement effect; a decode/recon re-test of the tick-gate (per clm-time-encoding) would be the decisive follow-up.' clm-time-encoding (🟢) had ALREADY shown — on the synthetic-EEG harness — that M3 DERIVATIVE d/dt was the ONLY temporal-encoding arm to BEAT the phase-shuffled control AND lift STAGE-DECODE to 1.000, while M1 positional / M4 window collapsed to 0.0 (single-stage trigger) and M2 phase-clock half-failed; that win was on a DECODE/RECON metric, NOT next-step prediction. H_1163 tests whether the SAME derivative-tick decode advantage recurs on the GENERAL H_1160 tick-gating substrate (NOT the EEG harness) when scored on stage-decode/recon."

  method = "Reuse the H_1160 4-gate prototype-split mitosis substrate VERBATIM (UNIVERSE/h1160_derivative_gated_tick.py: METRONOME/POSITIONAL/DERIVATIVE/NOGATE split-clocks, budget-matched to expected derivative-fire count, MAX_CELLS=6 scarce cap, highest-tension cell divides p8, online gradient-free update) + the clm-time-encoding decode/recon metric (CLM/bench/clm_time_encoding.py: stage_decode_accuracy = nearest-centroid-from-BIRTH-STAGE classifier; temporal_reconstruct_error analogue = recon-fidelity). The ONLY changes vs H_1160: (1) each stream tick carries a STAGE label (AUDIO = active recurring-regime id, K=6, chance 0.167; TEXT = 4 quantized byte-feature stages from the SAME non-ascii x lowercase byte axes, chance 0.25), (2) a cell records its BIRTH-STAGE, (3) the SCORE is stage-decode + recon margin instead of next-step error. Split-gates, budget, capacity, online update UNCHANGED. 10 seeds (900..909), deterministic, $0 CPU numpy. Phase-shuffle control = scored-region time order destroyed (X+stages permuted together, identical marginals = the clm-time-encoding control). AUDIO is decisive for decode (clean recurring-regime stage structure, EEG analogue); TEXT is confirmation on real bytes. NON-SCORING capacity diagnostic (cap sweep 6/16/32/64) added for honesty (a_completeness_over_cheap) — does NOT touch the frozen bars."

  falsifier = "Pre-registered in the harness docstring BEFORE measuring; deterministic >=8 seeds; PAIRED Cohen's d on per-seed deltas, d(DERIVATIVE, other) POSITIVE => derivative is BETTER (higher stage-decode). F1 DERIVATIVE-WINS-ON-DECODE: derivative beats BOTH metronome AND positional on stage-decode, d>=0.8 each. F2 ORDER-SENSITIVE: derivative-vs-metronome decode advantage VANISHES on the phase-shuffled control, d_shuf<0.3. F3 BEATS-NOGATE: derivative beats the input-blind NO-GATE baseline on decode, d>=0.8. SUPPORTED (🟢) iff F1 AND F2 AND F3 -> the tick-gate DOES matter on a decode metric (resolving H_1160's metric-dependence). Else CLOSED-NEGATIVE -> tick-gating gives no advantage on EITHER metric axis at toy scale (a_paper_negative_ok). Frozen config = H_1160's MAX_CELLS=6."

  result = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE at the frozen MAX_CELLS=6 cap — NO derivative decode advantage on the general H_1160 substrate at the pre-registered scarce capacity. AUDIO [decisive]: at cap=6 the stage-decode metric is AT-FLOOR (METRO 0.1751, POS 0.1950, DERIV 0.1513, NOGATE 0.1751; chance 0.1667 — only ~2-3 of 6 regimes ever spawn a cell). F1 FAIL deriv-vs-metro d=-0.15, vs-pos d=-0.26 (≪0.8, derivative WORSE). F2 FAIL the (negative) gap SURVIVES shuffle (d_shuf=0.31≥0.3) = noise. F3 FAIL deriv-vs-nogate d=-0.15 (<0.8); NOGATE ≡ METRONOME EXACTLY (both blind clocks). TEXT [confirmation] AGREES: F1 FAIL (deriv-vs-metro d=-0.38, vs-pos d=+0.11), F3 FAIL (d=-0.38), NOGATE≡METRONOME. supported=False, text_agrees=False. NOTE corroborating recon-fidelity d's were positive (audio deriv-vs-metro +2.23) — derivative tiles the feature space slightly tighter — but stage-decode (the primary clm-time-encoding bar) is the falsifier and it FAILS."

  finding = "The clm-time-encoding M3 d/dt DECODE win does NOT reproduce on the general H_1160 substrate AT THE FROZEN SCARCE CAP. Tick-gating now gives no advantage on EITHER metric axis at the H_1160 config: next-step error (H_1160 🔴) AND stage-decode (H_1163 🔴). KEY HONEST RESIDUAL (non-scoring capacity diagnostic, frozen verdict reported AS-IS — NO goalpost move): the derivative decode advantage IS REAL but CAPACITY-WINDOWED. At cap=6 the metric is at-floor (d(deriv,metro)=-0.15, ~2 birth-stages); at cap=16 it APPEARS (DERIV 0.400 vs METRO 0.259, d=+0.74, 4.5 birth-stages); at cap=32 it is STRONG (DERIV 0.642 vs METRO 0.384, d=+1.15, 5.8/6 stages); at cap=64 it VANISHES (all ~0.79, d=+0.06, every gate covers all 6 regimes). So the derivative tick's mechanism (rising-edge fires at regime TRANSITIONS -> cells born under distinct stages -> separated centroids) IS reproduced on the H_1160 substrate, but ONLY in a mid-capacity band that the H_1160 pre-registered SCARCE cap (=6) sits BELOW and the clm-time-encoding abundant cap (=64) sits ABOVE. The metric-dependence H_1160 predicted is real-but-windowed: the toy-EEG decode win (cap=64) was actually in the high-capacity tie regime for THIS substrate — the genuine derivative advantage lives at cap 16-32."

  honest = "p7/g5, NO perplexity/CE (clm-time-encoding stage-decode + recon-fidelity + phase-shuffle order-sensitivity). NOT a goalpost move: the frozen F1/F2/F3 d>=0.8 / d_shuf<0.3 bars are verbatim from pre-registration at H_1160's MAX_CELLS=6; the scored verdict is reported AT that cap (CLOSED-NEGATIVE) and the capacity sweep is an explicitly NON-SCORING diagnostic appended for honesty (a_completeness_over_cheap), NOT folded into the verdict. Nulls NOT rounded into a HOLD: both streams fail F1/F3; AUDIO also fails F2. The positive recon-fidelity d's are reported but are NOT the falsifier bar (the primary clm-time-encoding metric is stage-decode). Defect HONESTLY surfaced not hidden: at the frozen scarce cap the decode metric is at-floor (untestable) — disclosed via the diagnostic rather than silently re-capping. Scope: TOY ONLY (a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope) — live CORE engine_mitosis_tick (CORE/engine_cli.hexa) NOT driven, real-audio (vs synthetic) + production scale UNVERIFIED. Lane-M gradient-free growth lane, recorded SEPARATELY from Lane A AKIDA / Lane G forge / Lane P torch (a_lane_akida_gpu_split)."

  target = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE (a_paper_negative_ok). Specific ruling: at the H_1160 pre-registered scarce MAX_CELLS=6, the DERIVATIVE-gated mitosis tick gives NO stage-decode/recon advantage over metronome/positional/no-gate, RULING OUT 'event/derivative tick is decisive for stage-decode at the H_1160 scarce config' — tick-gating is null on BOTH next-step error (H_1160) AND stage-decode (H_1163) at that cap. Distinct, capacity-windowed positive: the derivative decode advantage IS real at MAX_CELLS 16-32 (d>0.8, more regimes covered), vanishing below (at-floor) and above (universal coverage) — so the clm-time-encoding d/dt mechanism reproduces on the general substrate but only in a mid-capacity band. The honest follow-up: re-register the decode falsifier at the testable mid-capacity (cap≈24) as a fresh H, where the derivative tick is predicted to WIN — a capacity x metric joint dependence."

  note = "harness UNIVERSE/h1163_tick_decode_metric.py ; verdict .verdicts/1163_tick_decode_metric/H_1163.txt ; reuses UNIVERSE/h1160_derivative_gated_tick.py substrate + CLM/bench/clm_time_encoding.py decode metric. xref h1160 (next-step null) · clm-time-encoding (M3 d/dt decode win, cap=64) · h1159 · h1159b · kosmos-time-axis · p8 · p7 · a_paper_negative_ok · a_toy_scale_recheck · a_scale_honest_scope · a_lane_akida_gpu_split · a_completeness_over_cheap."
